## 3. RENDERING ENGINE

### 3.1 Per-word optical tracking
`computeLockupLayout()` measures `w1` with `tracking1Em × fontSize` and `w2` with `tracking2Em × fontSize`. Both renderers apply the matching `letter-spacing`. Widths, centering and the safe-crop fit must use the tracked widths.

### 3.2 TLD rendering by `extStyle` (when `keepExt`)
Layout returns a typed `ext` block with a `mode` field instead of the hard-coded `extPill`. Keep the field name `extPill` as an alias, so existing consumers don't break.
- `inline` — baseline text after `w2`, color `accent`, weight 700, same size as `w2`.
- `superscript` — 38% size, weight 800, color `accent`, raised so its cap height aligns with the wordmark's cap height, gap 0.12em.
- `pill` — current behaviour (unchanged).
- `dot` — current `dot-badge` circle in `accent`, followed by the TLD text in `secondary` (the dot replaces the period).
- `tech-tag` — outlined rounded rect (`rx` 4 at 750px width, scaled), stroke `accent` 1.5, uppercase JetBrains Mono 34% size, weight 700, fill `accent`.

All five modes are measured, so the lockup stays centred and inside the Atom 80% safe zone.

### 3.3 Wordmark surgery (`wordmarkAccent`)
- `spark-dot`: an accent node in `accent` (circle `r = 0.09 × capHeight`, or a 45° diamond when the font is geometric/mono), placed at the junction of `w1` and `w2`, top-aligned to cap height. Position it from the measured `w1` width; never from hard-coded coordinates.
- `stencil-slice-45`: a 45° diagonal gap cut through the first glyph of `w1`. Build it with an SVG `<mask>`: a white rect plus a black rotated rectangle, `id` unique per render (`ls-stencil-${hash}`). A `clipPath` cannot subtract, so do not use one. Measure the first glyph's box with canvas `measureText` (`actualBoundingBoxAscent/Left/Right`) for the current font. Draw a complementary wedge in `accent` offset 2px along the cut. Canvas renderer: same result with `globalCompositeOperation = 'destination-out'` on an offscreen layer.

### 3.4 Compound emblems (`emblemFusion`), inside the emblem coordinate space used by `buildEmblemInnerMarkup()`
- `single` — current behaviour.
- `monogram-negative` — the uppercase initial of `word1` in the brand font at weight 900, set inside the construction as a large background glyph. Use the construction's contrast color at 22% opacity, or knock it out of the container with a mask when the construction is a solid shape. The primary icon sits in the foreground, scaled to 70% of the normal icon box, with its contrast guaranteed by `ensureIconContrast()`.
- `dual-badge` — the primary icon as today, plus a satellite badge at the container's top-right corner. The satellite is a circle in `accent`, with a ring the color of the current surface (white/dark/transparent → none), radius 16% of the emblem. Inside it sits `secondaryIcon`, scaled to 60% of the badge diameter, stroke `#05070B` or white (whichever passes contrast). Compute all coordinates from the construction's bounding box, never fixed numbers.

### 3.5 Motion (`motionPreset`) — SVG only
When `motionPreset !== 'none'`, `generateFullLogoSvg(state, { …, animated: true })` adds `class` hooks (`ls-emblem`, `ls-glyph`, `ls-word`, `ls-spark`) and a `<style>` block with the keyframes, so the downloaded `.svg` animates on its own.
- `draw-stroke`: every stroked icon element gets `pathLength="1"`, `stroke-dasharray: 1`, `stroke-dashoffset: 1 → 0` over 0.95s `cubic-bezier(0.16,1,0.3,1)`. Do not use a fixed 140 dash length. The words reveal with opacity + 10px translateX after 0.18s, and the spark pulses with `scale(1.24)` every 2.2s (`transform-box: fill-box; transform-origin: center`).
- `kinetic-spin`: the emblem goes from `rotate(-18deg) scale(.82)` to `rotate(4deg) scale(1.03)` to rest, over 0.8s `cubic-bezier(0.34,1.56,0.64,1)`.
- `ambient-pulse`: the emblem breathes on a 2.8s loop (opacity 1 → .88, translateY 0 → -1.5px).
- Wrap all of it in `@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { animation: none !important; } }`.
- PNG exports are always static (final frame).
- The live Master Canvas plays the animation through an inline SVG preview with a "Replay" button.

### 3.6 Self-contained SVG fonts (fixes current exports)
Replace the `@import` in `generateFullLogoSvg()` with embedded fonts, for every exported or copied SVG:
1. Fetch the Google Fonts CSS for the family and the weights actually used, with `&text=` set to the exact characters rendered (w1 + w2 + ext + tagline + monogram). This returns a tiny subset.
2. Fetch the referenced `woff2` and embed it as `@font-face { src: url(data:font/woff2;base64,…) }`.
3. Cache by `family|weight|text` in memory.
4. On network failure, fall back to the current `@import` and show a toast saying the SVG needs internet to render its font.

Make `generateFullLogoSvg` async (`generateFullLogoSvgEmbedded`), or keep the sync version for the live preview and add an async export wrapper. All download, copy and ZIP paths must use the embedded version.

